NimbyEarplugs (Ears) - original work by Jeff Fabish for NIMBY | HARDCORE | BADLANDS | 1pp.
Modifies the vanilla DayZ 1.30 MissionBase, MissionGameplay, and NotificationUI classes
(Bohemia Interactive) to toggle the scene effect volume; no third-party mod code.

Changes, newest first:

- October 27, 2026, release-1 patch 1 (plan v0.12, E15, branch
  fix/release-1-patch-1, from the October 27 review, row 21): the launch
  value is the DeferredInit cache (g_Game.m_volume_sound) when it is
  populated and the live channel only when that cache reads 0, so a rejoin
  after a death-screen or unconscious exit in the same client process no
  longer starts from a channel that death left at 0 (NimbyEarplugsLevel
  .PickBaseline, two self-test cases, 28 total); the loaded line carries
  launch_from=cache|scene. The toggle input is held as the persistent
  wrapper (UAIDWrapper, UAInput.c:99, :29) and re-resolved on each read, so
  an Options > Controls rebind takes effect without a relog (EP-005 re-run
  on the cached-input build is the test).
- October 21, 2026, release-1 round (E14 revised by Jeff on the measured
  rows, findings NIMBY-T-018 and NIMBY-T-019 in the test record): the
  Effects slider read is gone; OnInit reads the launch value of the scene
  effect channel once, earplugs in writes 0.15 of it, take-out and the
  mission-finish take-out write it back. The loaded, toggle, sample, and
  reapply lines carry launch_sound=; the logout menu is named; one
  self-test case for the launch-value restore (26 total).
- October 21, 2026, release-1 round (second commit): the saved level is read
  from the stored value of the Effects slider (GameOptions, resolved once in
  OnInit) when that accessor resolves; the m_volume_sound path with the
  captured fallback stays behind it. Toggle, sample, and reapply lines carry
  slider=.
- October 21, 2026, release-1 round: the toggle key is ignored while any
  scripted menu is open (chat input included, E12) and while the player is
  dead or unconscious; the saved-level fallback is captured once while
  earplugs are out and held while they are in, as a pure function in
  NimbyEarplugsLevel (E13); TakeOut clears the suppressed state; the UAInput
  is resolved once in OnInit; the per-second sample line is built only under
  the debug flag; earplugs come out in OnMissionFinish; nine new self-test
  cases (25 total); reapply lines carry the saved and scene levels.
- October 21, 2026: the self-test completion line prints the case count,
  "[NIMBY][Earplugs] selftest complete; cases=N failures=M", so the
  Build-NimbyPack boot check can fail a self-test that ran no cases or
  stayed silent. No change to what Ears does in game.
- October 19, 2026: Inputs.xml nests <sorting> inside <inputs>, so the binding
  shows on the shared NIMBY tab in Options > Controls (NIMBY-T-007).
- October 17, 2026: Phase 0 and Phase 1 in-game PASS; the vanilla notification
  toast leak is fixed in NotificationUI (E4) and Inputs.xml gains its sorting
  tag (E11).
- October 16, 2026, Phase 1: the toggle reapplies the reduced level whenever
  the scene volume drifts (E7-E10); 16 engine-free self-test cases.
- October 16, 2026, Phase 0: N toggles the scene effect volume and logs the
  vanilla reset points; the pack.json row lands with a stub addon.
